<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa welcomes pact between unions.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa welcomes pact between unions.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Deutsche Lufthansa AG on Tuesday welcomed the decision by the DAG trade union to work together with the OeTV union to resolve its pay dispute with the carrier.</p>
<p>Lufthansa chief executive Juergen Weber said reporters the decision proved that the unions were looking to the future.</p>
<p>&quot;I am sure that this decision will bolster Lufthansa,&quot; Weber said, in comments passed on by the Lufthansa press office.</p>
<p>The DAG also said it would accept a wage agreement struck between the OeTV and Lufthsansa last October.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
